+# How a Genkit flow streams output to a caller
+
+Source: inspected locally installed packages (`@genkit-ai/core`, `genkit`) in
+`node_modules` — the Genkit MCP docs server was unavailable (connection closed).
+
+## Defining a streaming flow (producer side)
+
+Use `ai.defineFlow()` with a `streamSchema` in the config. The flow function
+receives a second argument — the streaming callback (also called a "side
+channel") — and calls it with each chunk as it's produced.
+
+- Config option: `streamSchema` (in addition to `inputSchema`/`outputSchema`)
+- Callback argument to the flow function: `(input, streamingCallback) => ...`
+  (also exposed as `sendChunk` when destructured from the context arg)
+
+```ts
+export const flowStreamExample = ai.defineFlow(
+  {
+    name: 'flowStreamExample',
+    inputSchema: z.string(),
+    streamSchema: z.string(),
+    outputSchema: z.string(),
+  },
+  async (prompt, { sendChunk }) => {
+    const { response, stream } = ai.generateStream({
+      model: googleAI.model('gemini-2.5-flash'),
+      prompt,
+    });
+
+    for await (const chunk of stream) {
+      // forward each chunk to the caller
+      sendChunk(chunk.text);
+    }
+
+    return (await response).text;
+  }
+);
+```
+
+## Consuming a streaming flow (caller side)
+
+### In-process (same Node process)
+
+Every defined flow is an `Action`, which exposes a `.stream()` method:
+
+```ts
+const { stream, output } = flowStreamExample.stream('tell me a joke');
+
+for await (const chunk of stream) {
+  console.log(chunk);
+}
+
+console.log(await output); // final, full output
+```
+
+`.stream()` returns `{ stream: AsyncGenerator<Chunk>, output: Promise<Output> }`.
+
+### Over HTTP (deployed flow, e.g. via `genkit/beta/client`)
+
+Use `streamFlow()`:
+
+```ts
+import { streamFlow } from 'genkit/beta/client';
+
+const response = streamFlow({
+  url: 'https://my-flow-deployed-url',
+  input: 'foo',
+});
+
+for await (const chunk of response.stream) {
+  console.log(chunk);
+}
+
+console.log(await response.output);
+```
+
+(The non-streaming HTTP equivalent is `runFlow()`.)
+
+## Summary of function names
+
+| Side | In-process | Deployed/HTTP |
+|---|---|---|
+| Define | `ai.defineFlow({ streamSchema, ... }, (input, { sendChunk }) => ...)` | same |
+| Call | `flow.stream(input)` → `{ stream, output }` | `streamFlow({ url, input })` → `{ stream, output, streamId }` |
